module

public import MathlibExt.Probability.Causality.CausalIdentification

/-!
# Double robustness of the augmented inverse probability weighted (AIPW) score

Binary treatment (an event `T`), potential outcomes `Y₀, Y₁`, an observed outcome `Y`, and
covariate information given by a sub-σ-algebra `m` (for example the σ-algebra generated by a
covariate `X`). Write `e* = P(T | m)` for the true propensity score and `μ₀* = E[Y₀ | m]`,
`μ₁* = E[Y₁ | m]` for the true outcome regressions. For *fixed* candidate nuisances (an
`m`-measurable propensity `e` and `m`-measurable outcome regressions `g₀, g₁`), the AIPW score is
`ψ = g₁ - g₀ + 1_T (Y - g₁) / e - 1_{Tᶜ} (Y - g₀) / (1 - e)`.

## Main definitions

* `aipwScoreOfSigma T Y e g₀ g₁`: the AIPW score above, for an arbitrary observed outcome `Y`,
  with nuisances given as `m`-measurable functions on `Ω`. It is a separate name from the
  covariate-indexed AIPW score of task CAUS-02.1 (`aipwScore T X Y e m₀ m₁`, nuisances functions
  of the covariate value): that score is, by unfolding the definitions (`rfl`),
  `aipwScoreOfSigma T Y (e ∘ X) (m₀ ∘ X) (m₁ ∘ X)`, to be used with `m := MeasurableSpace.comap X`.

## Main results

* `integral_aipwScoreOfSigma_sub`: the exact bias identity (a product of nuisance errors),
  `E[ψ] - E[Y₁ - Y₀] = E[(e* - e) ((μ₁* - g₁) / e + (μ₀* - g₀) / (1 - e))]`.
* `integral_aipwScoreOfSigma_of_propensity`: `E[ψ] = E[Y₁ - Y₀]` when the propensity is correct,
  `e = e*` a.e., for any outcome regressions.
* `integral_aipwScoreOfSigma_of_outcome`: `E[ψ] = E[Y₁ - Y₀]` when both outcome regressions are
  correct, `g₀ = μ₀*` and `g₁ = μ₁*` a.e., for any propensity.
* `integrable_aipwScoreOfSigma`: the score is integrable.

## Hypotheses

All assumptions are explicit hypotheses of the theorems:
* *consistency*: `Y = 1_T Y₁ + 1_{Tᶜ} Y₀` a.e. (`observed T Y₀ Y₁`);
* *mean exchangeability*: `E[1_T Y₁ | m] = e* μ₁*` and `E[1_{Tᶜ} Y₀ | m] = (1 - e*) μ₀*` a.e.
  (implied by `(Y₀, Y₁) ⊥ T | m`);
* *bounded inverse weights*: `ε ≤ e ≤ 1 - ε` a.e. for some `ε > 0`. When the propensity is
  correct this is strong positivity of the true propensity, `ε ≤ e* ≤ 1 - ε`. Positivity of `e*`
  is not needed for the identity itself, nor for the outcome-correct case; without it, however,
  `μ₀*, μ₁*` are not identified from the law of the observed data;
* *integrability*: `Y₀, Y₁, g₀, g₁` are integrable and `e, g₀, g₁` are `m`-strongly measurable.

## Scope: population level, fixed nuisances

Every statement is about the population expectation of the score at **fixed** candidate
nuisances `e, g₀, g₁`. Nothing here asserts finite-sample unbiasedness of an AIPW *estimator*: when
the nuisances are fitted on the same sample on which the score is averaged, they depend on the
data and the identities below do not apply. Sample splitting, cross-fitting and the
`n^{-1/2}`-rate analysis of the product remainder are not covered.

## Source receipt (API-00)

* Reuse search (2026-11-11, base `53666a3c1`): no AIPW, augmented IPW or doubly robust
  development in Mathlib (`v4.35.0`) or in this repository. Reused: `observed` (consistency) from
  `MathlibExt.Probability.Causality.CausalIdentification`, whose
  `integral_ipw_treated_condExp` is the pure-IPW special case; Mathlib's pull-out property
  `condExp_mul_of_stronglyMeasurable_left`.
* Checked against: E. H. Kennedy, *Semiparametric doubly robust targeted double machine
  learning: a review*, arXiv:2203.06469v2 (2023), §3.2, Example 2 (continued), and §4.3. The
  remainder there for the treated-arm mean `E{E(Y | X, A = 1)}` is
  `R₂(P̄, P) = ∫ (1/π̄ - 1/π)(μ - μ̄) π dP`, i.e. `∫ (π - π̄)(μ - μ̄) / π̄ dP`; with `π̄ = e`,
  `μ̄ = g₁` this is the treated-arm term of `integral_aipwScoreOfSigma_sub`, and the control arm
  is the same formula for `A ↦ 1 - A`. §4.3 uses the same bound `π̂ ≥ ε` on the candidate
  propensity.

## References

* J. M. Robins, A. Rotnitzky and L. P. Zhao, *Estimation of regression coefficients when some
  regressors are not always observed*, JASA 89(427) (1994), 846–866.
* H. Bang and J. M. Robins, *Doubly robust estimation in missing data and causal inference
  models*, Biometrics 61(4) (2005), 962–973.
* E. H. Kennedy, *Semiparametric doubly robust targeted double machine learning: a review*,
  arXiv:2203.06469 (2023).
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.Probability.Causality

open MeasureTheory

variable {Ω : Type*} {mΩ : MeasurableSpace Ω} {μ : Measure Ω}

/-- The augmented inverse probability weighted (AIPW) score with candidate propensity `e` and
candidate outcome regressions `g₀, g₁`, at the observed outcome `Y`:
`g₁ - g₀ + 1_T (Y - g₁) / e - 1_{Tᶜ} (Y - g₀) / (1 - e)`. -/
noncomputable def aipwScoreOfSigma (T : Set Ω) (Y e g₀ g₁ : Ω → ℝ) : Ω → ℝ := fun ω =>
  g₁ ω - g₀ ω + T.indicator (fun ω => (Y ω - g₁ ω) / e ω) ω -
    Tᶜ.indicator (fun ω => (Y ω - g₀ ω) / (1 - e ω)) ω

/-- One arm of the AIPW score, `f + 1_S (Z - f) / p`, is integrable when `Z, f` are and
`p ≥ ε > 0`. -/
private lemma integrable_arm {S : Set Ω} (hS : MeasurableSet S) {Z f p : Ω → ℝ}
    (hZ : Integrable Z μ) (hfi : Integrable f μ) (hp : AEStronglyMeasurable p μ) {ε : ℝ}
    (hε : 0 < ε) (hpε : ∀ᵐ ω ∂μ, ε ≤ p ω) :
    Integrable (fun ω => f ω + S.indicator (fun ω => (Z ω - f ω) / p ω) ω) μ := by
  have hbdd : ∀ᵐ ω ∂μ, ‖(p ω)⁻¹‖ ≤ ε⁻¹ := hpε.mono fun ω hω => by
    rw [Real.norm_eq_abs, abs_inv, abs_of_pos (hε.trans_le hω)]
    exact inv_anti₀ hε hω
  refine hfi.add ((((hZ.sub hfi).bdd_mul hp.aemeasurable.inv.aestronglyMeasurable hbdd).indicator
    hS).congr (Filter.Eventually.of_forall fun ω => ?_))
  by_cases hω : ω ∈ S <;> simp [hω, div_eq_inv_mul]

/-- One arm of the AIPW score, `f + 1_S (Z - f) / p`, with `q = P(S | m)`: it is integrable and
`E[f + 1_S (Z - f) / p] - E[Z] = E[(q - p) (E[Z | m] - f) / p]`, the right side integrable. -/
private lemma aipw_arm {m : MeasurableSpace Ω} (hm : m ≤ mΩ) [IsFiniteMeasure μ] {S : Set Ω}
    (hS : MeasurableSet[mΩ] S) {Z f p : Ω → ℝ} (hZ : Integrable Z μ) (hf : StronglyMeasurable[m] f)
    (hfi : Integrable f μ) (hp : StronglyMeasurable[m] p) {ε : ℝ} (hε : 0 < ε)
    (hpε : ∀ᵐ ω ∂μ, ε ≤ p ω)
    (hex : μ[S.indicator Z | m] =ᵐ[μ] μ[S.indicator 1 | m] * μ[Z | m]) :
    Integrable (fun ω => f ω + S.indicator (fun ω => (Z ω - f ω) / p ω) ω) μ ∧
    Integrable (fun ω => (μ[S.indicator 1 | m] ω - p ω) * (μ[Z | m] ω - f ω) / p ω) μ ∧
    ∫ ω, (f ω + S.indicator (fun ω => (Z ω - f ω) / p ω) ω) ∂μ - ∫ ω, Z ω ∂μ =
      ∫ ω, (μ[S.indicator 1 | m] ω - p ω) * (μ[Z | m] ω - f ω) / p ω ∂μ := by
  set r : Ω → ℝ := fun ω => (p ω)⁻¹
  have hr : StronglyMeasurable[m] r := hp.measurable.inv.stronglyMeasurable
  have hbdd : ∀ᵐ ω ∂μ, ‖r ω‖ ≤ ε⁻¹ := hpε.mono fun ω hω => by
    rw [Real.norm_eq_abs, abs_inv, abs_of_pos (hε.trans_le hω)]
    exact inv_anti₀ hε hω
  have hSZ : Integrable (S.indicator Z) μ := hZ.indicator hS
  have hS1 : Integrable (S.indicator (1 : Ω → ℝ)) μ := (integrable_const 1).indicator hS
  have h1 : Integrable (r * S.indicator Z) μ :=
    hSZ.bdd_mul (hr.mono hm).aestronglyMeasurable hbdd
  have hrf : Integrable (r * f) μ := hfi.bdd_mul (hr.mono hm).aestronglyMeasurable hbdd
  have h2 : Integrable (r * f * S.indicator 1) μ := by
    refine (hrf.indicator hS).congr (Filter.Eventually.of_forall fun ω => ?_)
    by_cases hω : ω ∈ S <;> simp [hω]
  have harm : (fun ω => f ω + S.indicator (fun ω => (Z ω - f ω) / p ω) ω) =
      f + (r * S.indicator Z - r * f * S.indicator 1) := by
    funext ω
    by_cases hω : ω ∈ S
    · simp [hω, r, div_eq_inv_mul]; ring
    · simp [hω]
  have hA := condExp_mul_of_stronglyMeasurable_left hr h1 hSZ
  have hB := condExp_mul_of_stronglyMeasurable_left (hr.mul hf) h2 hS1
  have hAB : Integrable (f + (μ[r * S.indicator Z | m] - μ[r * f * S.indicator 1 | m]) -
      μ[Z | m]) μ :=
    (hfi.add (integrable_condExp.sub integrable_condExp)).sub integrable_condExp
  have hcongr : f + (μ[r * S.indicator Z | m] - μ[r * f * S.indicator 1 | m]) - μ[Z | m] =ᵐ[μ]
      fun ω => (μ[S.indicator 1 | m] ω - p ω) * (μ[Z | m] ω - f ω) / p ω := by
    filter_upwards [hA, hB, hex, hpε] with ω hA hB hex hpε
    have hp0 : p ω ≠ 0 := (hε.trans_le hpε).ne'
    simp only [Pi.add_apply, Pi.sub_apply, Pi.mul_apply] at hA hB hex ⊢
    rw [hA, hB, hex]
    simp only [r]
    field_simp
    ring
  refine ⟨integrable_arm hS hZ hfi (hp.mono hm).aestronglyMeasurable hε hpε, hAB.congr hcongr, ?_⟩
  rw [harm, ← integral_congr_ae hcongr, integral_sub' (hfi.add (integrable_condExp.sub
    integrable_condExp)) integrable_condExp, integral_add' hfi (integrable_condExp.sub
    integrable_condExp), integral_sub' integrable_condExp integrable_condExp, integral_condExp hm,
    integral_condExp hm, integral_condExp hm, integral_add' hfi (h1.sub h2), integral_sub' h1 h2]

/-- `P(Tᶜ | m) = 1 - P(T | m)`. -/
private lemma condExp_indicator_compl_one {m : MeasurableSpace Ω} (hm : m ≤ mΩ)
    [IsFiniteMeasure μ] {T : Set Ω} (hT : MeasurableSet[mΩ] T) :
    μ[Tᶜ.indicator (1 : Ω → ℝ) | m] =ᵐ[μ] fun ω => 1 - μ[T.indicator 1 | m] ω := by
  have hc : Tᶜ.indicator (1 : Ω → ℝ) = (fun _ => (1 : ℝ)) - T.indicator 1 := by
    rw [Set.indicator_compl]; rfl
  have h1 : Integrable (fun _ => (1 : ℝ)) μ := integrable_const 1
  have hT1 : Integrable (T.indicator (1 : Ω → ℝ)) μ := (integrable_const (1 : ℝ)).indicator hT
  rw [hc]
  filter_upwards [condExp_sub h1 hT1 m] with ω h
  rw [h, Pi.sub_apply, condExp_const hm]

/-- Consistency rewrites the score as the difference of the two arms evaluated at the potential
outcomes. -/
private lemma aipwScoreOfSigma_ae_eq {T : Set Ω} {Y Y₀ Y₁ : Ω → ℝ}
    (hcons : Y =ᵐ[μ] observed T Y₀ Y₁) (e g₀ g₁ : Ω → ℝ) :
    aipwScoreOfSigma T Y e g₀ g₁ =ᵐ[μ] fun ω =>
      (g₁ ω + T.indicator (fun ω => (Y₁ ω - g₁ ω) / e ω) ω) -
        (g₀ ω + Tᶜ.indicator (fun ω => (Y₀ ω - g₀ ω) / (1 - e ω)) ω) := by
  filter_upwards [hcons] with ω h
  by_cases hω : ω ∈ T <;> simp [aipwScoreOfSigma, observed, h, hω] <;> ring

variable {m : MeasurableSpace Ω} [IsFiniteMeasure μ] {T : Set Ω} {Y Y₀ Y₁ e g₀ g₁ : Ω → ℝ}
  {ε : ℝ}

omit [IsFiniteMeasure μ] in
/-- The AIPW score with candidate nuisances `e, g₀, g₁` is integrable, under consistency,
integrable potential outcomes and candidate regressions, and `ε ≤ e ≤ 1 - ε`. -/
theorem integrable_aipwScoreOfSigma (hT : MeasurableSet[mΩ] T)
    (hcons : Y =ᵐ[μ] observed T Y₀ Y₁) (hY₀ : Integrable Y₀ μ) (hY₁ : Integrable Y₁ μ)
    (he : AEStronglyMeasurable[mΩ] e μ)
    (hg₀i : Integrable g₀ μ) (hg₁i : Integrable g₁ μ) (hε : 0 < ε)
    (heε : ∀ᵐ ω ∂μ, ε ≤ e ω ∧ e ω ≤ 1 - ε) :
    Integrable (aipwScoreOfSigma T Y e g₀ g₁) μ :=
  ((integrable_arm hT hY₁ hg₁i he hε (heε.mono fun _ h => h.1)).sub
    (integrable_arm (p := fun ω => 1 - e ω) hT.compl hY₀ hg₀i (aestronglyMeasurable_const.sub he)
      hε (heε.mono fun _ h => by linarith [h.2]))).congr
    (aipwScoreOfSigma_ae_eq hcons e g₀ g₁).symm

/-- **Exact bias of the AIPW score** (a product of nuisance errors). Let `e* = P(T | m)`,
`μ₀* = E[Y₀ | m]` and `μ₁* = E[Y₁ | m]`. Under consistency, mean exchangeability, integrability
and `ε ≤ e ≤ 1 - ε`, for fixed `m`-measurable candidates `e, g₀, g₁`,
`E[ψ] - E[Y₁ - Y₀] = E[(e* - e) ((μ₁* - g₁) / e + (μ₀* - g₀) / (1 - e))]`.
This is a population identity at fixed nuisances, not a finite-sample statement about fitted
nuisances. -/
theorem integral_aipwScoreOfSigma_sub (hm : m ≤ mΩ) (hT : MeasurableSet[mΩ] T)
    (hcons : Y =ᵐ[μ] observed T Y₀ Y₁) (hY₀ : Integrable Y₀ μ) (hY₁ : Integrable Y₁ μ)
    (hex₁ : μ[T.indicator Y₁ | m] =ᵐ[μ] μ[T.indicator 1 | m] * μ[Y₁ | m])
    (hex₀ : μ[Tᶜ.indicator Y₀ | m] =ᵐ[μ] (1 - μ[T.indicator 1 | m]) * μ[Y₀ | m])
    (he : StronglyMeasurable[m] e) (hg₀ : StronglyMeasurable[m] g₀)
    (hg₁ : StronglyMeasurable[m] g₁) (hg₀i : Integrable g₀ μ) (hg₁i : Integrable g₁ μ)
    (hε : 0 < ε) (heε : ∀ᵐ ω ∂μ, ε ≤ e ω ∧ e ω ≤ 1 - ε) :
    ∫ ω, aipwScoreOfSigma T Y e g₀ g₁ ω ∂μ - ∫ ω, (Y₁ ω - Y₀ ω) ∂μ =
      ∫ ω, (μ[T.indicator 1 | m] ω - e ω) *
        ((μ[Y₁ | m] ω - g₁ ω) / e ω + (μ[Y₀ | m] ω - g₀ ω) / (1 - e ω)) ∂μ := by
  have hq₀ := condExp_indicator_compl_one (μ := μ) hm hT
  obtain ⟨hA₁, hR₁, h₁⟩ := aipw_arm hm hT hY₁ hg₁ hg₁i he hε (heε.mono fun _ h => h.1) hex₁
  obtain ⟨hA₀, hR₀, h₀⟩ := aipw_arm (p := fun ω => 1 - e ω) hm hT.compl hY₀ hg₀ hg₀i
    (stronglyMeasurable_const.sub he) hε
    (heε.mono fun _ h => by linarith [h.2]) (by
      filter_upwards [hex₀, hq₀] with ω h h'
      rw [h, Pi.mul_apply, Pi.mul_apply, h', Pi.sub_apply, Pi.one_apply])
  rw [integral_congr_ae (aipwScoreOfSigma_ae_eq hcons e g₀ g₁), integral_sub hA₁ hA₀,
    integral_sub hY₁ hY₀,
    show ∀ a b c d : ℝ, a - b - (c - d) = (a - c) - (b - d) from fun _ _ _ _ => by ring, h₁, h₀,
    ← integral_sub hR₁ hR₀]
  refine integral_congr_ae ?_
  filter_upwards [hq₀] with ω h
  rw [h]
  ring

/-- **Double robustness, propensity correct**: if the candidate propensity is the true one,
`e = P(T | m)` a.e., the AIPW score is unbiased for the average treatment effect for *any*
candidate outcome regressions `g₀, g₁` (population level, fixed nuisances). -/
theorem integral_aipwScoreOfSigma_of_propensity (hm : m ≤ mΩ) (hT : MeasurableSet[mΩ] T)
    (hcons : Y =ᵐ[μ] observed T Y₀ Y₁) (hY₀ : Integrable Y₀ μ) (hY₁ : Integrable Y₁ μ)
    (hex₁ : μ[T.indicator Y₁ | m] =ᵐ[μ] μ[T.indicator 1 | m] * μ[Y₁ | m])
    (hex₀ : μ[Tᶜ.indicator Y₀ | m] =ᵐ[μ] (1 - μ[T.indicator 1 | m]) * μ[Y₀ | m])
    (he : StronglyMeasurable[m] e) (hg₀ : StronglyMeasurable[m] g₀)
    (hg₁ : StronglyMeasurable[m] g₁) (hg₀i : Integrable g₀ μ) (hg₁i : Integrable g₁ μ)
    (hε : 0 < ε) (heε : ∀ᵐ ω ∂μ, ε ≤ e ω ∧ e ω ≤ 1 - ε)
    (hprop : e =ᵐ[μ] μ[T.indicator 1 | m]) :
    ∫ ω, aipwScoreOfSigma T Y e g₀ g₁ ω ∂μ = ∫ ω, (Y₁ ω - Y₀ ω) ∂μ := by
  rw [← sub_eq_zero, integral_aipwScoreOfSigma_sub hm hT hcons hY₀ hY₁ hex₁ hex₀ he hg₀ hg₁ hg₀i
    hg₁i hε heε, ← integral_zero Ω ℝ]
  refine integral_congr_ae ?_
  filter_upwards [hprop] with ω h
  simp [h]

/-- **Double robustness, outcome regressions correct**: if `g₀ = E[Y₀ | m]` and
`g₁ = E[Y₁ | m]` a.e., the AIPW score is unbiased for the average treatment effect for *any*
candidate propensity `e` with `ε ≤ e ≤ 1 - ε` (population level, fixed nuisances). The true
propensity `e*` may reach `0` or `1` here, but then the correct regression `g₁ = μ₁*` (on
`{e* = 0}`) or `g₀ = μ₀*` (on `{e* = 1}`) is not identified from the law of the observed data. -/
theorem integral_aipwScoreOfSigma_of_outcome (hm : m ≤ mΩ) (hT : MeasurableSet[mΩ] T)
    (hcons : Y =ᵐ[μ] observed T Y₀ Y₁) (hY₀ : Integrable Y₀ μ) (hY₁ : Integrable Y₁ μ)
    (hex₁ : μ[T.indicator Y₁ | m] =ᵐ[μ] μ[T.indicator 1 | m] * μ[Y₁ | m])
    (hex₀ : μ[Tᶜ.indicator Y₀ | m] =ᵐ[μ] (1 - μ[T.indicator 1 | m]) * μ[Y₀ | m])
    (he : StronglyMeasurable[m] e) (hg₀ : StronglyMeasurable[m] g₀)
    (hg₁ : StronglyMeasurable[m] g₁) (hg₀i : Integrable g₀ μ) (hg₁i : Integrable g₁ μ)
    (hε : 0 < ε) (heε : ∀ᵐ ω ∂μ, ε ≤ e ω ∧ e ω ≤ 1 - ε)
    (hout₀ : g₀ =ᵐ[μ] μ[Y₀ | m]) (hout₁ : g₁ =ᵐ[μ] μ[Y₁ | m]) :
    ∫ ω, aipwScoreOfSigma T Y e g₀ g₁ ω ∂μ = ∫ ω, (Y₁ ω - Y₀ ω) ∂μ := by
  rw [← sub_eq_zero, integral_aipwScoreOfSigma_sub hm hT hcons hY₀ hY₁ hex₁ hex₀ he hg₀ hg₁ hg₀i
    hg₁i hε heε, ← integral_zero Ω ℝ]
  refine integral_congr_ae ?_
  filter_upwards [hout₀, hout₁] with ω h₀ h₁
  simp [h₀, h₁]

end MathlibExt.Probability.Causality
